  "response": "It sounds like you're going through a challenging time with your husband. It’s understandable to feel frustrated when similar concerns keep coming up. Engaging in self-care activities such as maintaining regular exercise, eating and sleeping habits, staying connected with friends and family, and talking to someone trusted about your feelings can be really beneficial for managing any stress or anxiety you might be experiencing. These steps can help you maintain a sense of well-being and might also improve the overall atmosphere within your relationship. If you ever feel overwhelmed, it's important to know that crisis resources are available. In the U.S., you can call the National Domestic Violence Hotline at 1-800-799-SAFE (7233) or text "START" to 88788 for confidential support.",
